{"name":"Commercial refrigeration controller alarm code lookup by brand","description":"What the alarm or fault code shown on a walk-in cooler/freezer digital temperature controller means, taken from each manufacturer's own manual. A restaurant or grocery refrigeration tech reads a short code off a Danfoss, Carel, or Dixell controller display and has to know which brand's board it is before the code means anything -- 'E03' is a digital-input alarm on a Carel IR33 and something else entirely on a different maker's board. Each record is one alarm/fault code from one manufacturer's controller: the code exactly as the display shows it, what it signals, and (where the manual states it) its effect on the outputs or its cause. A web search for 'walk-in cooler controller error codes' turns up only single-brand troubleshooting pages -- no cross-brand comparison exists, because each manufacturer publishes only its own controller's manual.","url":"https://referencesource.org/commercial-refrigeration-controller-alarm-codes-by-brand/","licence":"factual compilation from manufacturer technical manuals","last_verified":"2026-08-27","stale_after":"2028-08-26","sources":["https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/latest/54543/BC162786425567en-000901.pdf","https://docs.rs-online.com/f254/0900766b8111f52c.pdf","https://webapps.copeland.com/Dixell/Content/Pages/Manuals/XR-CHC/XR60CHC/XR60CHC-EN.pdf"],"records":[{"brand":"Danfoss","model_series":"EKC 202","alarm_code":"A1","alarm_meaning":"High temperature alarm","id":"ekc-202-danfoss-a1","url":"https://referencesource.org/commercial-refrigeration-controller-alarm-codes-by-brand/ekc-202-danfoss-a1/","source":"https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/latest/54543/BC162786425567en-000901.pdf","source_quote":"A1: High temperature alarm","verified_fields":["alarm_code","alarm_meaning","brand","model_series"]},{"brand":"Danfoss","model_series":"EKC 202","alarm_code":"A2","alarm_meaning":"Low temperature alarm","id":"ekc-202-danfoss-a2","url":"https:/